   75                   
   76                   / Channel status flags
   77                   / dsfopn - channel has been opened by scb
   78                   / dsfsvr - channel is a server channel, else client
   79                   / dsfcon - connected to remote host
   80                   / dsfful - socket transmit buffer is full
   81                   / dsfrdy - has characters ready to read
   82                   / dsfser - got a socket error of some kine
   83                   / dsfcls - remote closed connection
   84                   / dsfien - interrupts are enabled
   85                   / dsfior - interrupted because a character was received
   86                   / dsfioc - interrupted because a connection was opened or closed
   87                   / dsfioe - interrupted because transmit buffer full or other socket error
   88                   / dsfcur - is the current channel
   89                   
