  184                   
  185                   / Write a block of ascii text out.
  186                   / Write out a string produced by ascii until a word containing
  187                   / only 0 is seen, the starting address is in the ac,
  188                   / ascii <whatever>
  189                   /
  190                   / Include this before using it or declaring text that uses
  191                   / the character defines, below.
  192                   /
  193                   / Output goes to SBS channel 0 which must be in ascii mode.
  194                   / On call, AC contains the address of the text block.
  195                   / Insert this at the desired point in code.
  196                   / Call via jda txtasc.
  197                   
  198                   
  199                   
  200                   
